            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0672" n="556" xml:id="pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/4419: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-10-20T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20,
                                1923—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>226. Your telegram No. 321, September 22, 1 p.m.</p>
                <p>With reference to the request for releases of customs funds to the Canton
                    Government the Department maintains its previous position that the Diplomatic
                    Body deals with customs surpluses only as trustees for the recognized Government
                    of China.</p>
                <p>As to the proposed suppression of Custom Houses in territory controlled by Canton
                    and the levying on foreign merchandise of taxes in lieu of import and export
                    duties, this Government would of course regard such action as a subversion of
                    the treaty basis of foreign trade with China.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
